<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:ctrl="using:Remex.Desktop.Controls"
        xmlns:conv="using:Remex.Desktop.Converters"
        xmlns:material="clr-namespace:Material.Styles.Controls;assembly=Material.Styles"
        xmlns:mi="using:Material.Icons.Avalonia"
        xmlns:vm="using:Remex.Desktop.ViewModels">
    <!-- ═══ Spec B (RemEx-4kv0g.3): sensor cards paint from their palette family ═══

         Host classes (bound from the VM): family-primary / family-secondary / family-tertiary /
         family-neutral / family-custom. Part classes on the elements inside a card: sensor-title,
         card-value, card-value-2, card-unit, card-pill, card-plate, card-legend-plate, card-spark,
         card-legend-1, card-legend-2, card-legend-name, card-icon.

         THE ACTUAL AVALONIA PRECEDENCE RULE (whole-branch review — the earlier comment here said
         "registration order", which is only half of it). A selector that carries a class OR a
         pseudo-class (".family-primary", ".card-title", ":pointerover") is an *activated* style
         and resolves at BindingPriority.StyleTrigger; a selector with only element/type parts
         (plain "TextBlock", "ctrl|SparklineControl") resolves at the lower BindingPriority.Style.
         The higher tier ALWAYS wins, regardless of where either style is registered — that is why
         every rule in this file beats App.axaml's plain "TextBlock" and "ctrl|SparklineControl"
         styles even though those are declared later. Declaration/include order only decides a
         tie WITHIN the same tier. Two concrete cases this file has hit, both same-tier ties:
           - "sensor-title", NOT "card-title" (fix round 1). App.axaml's global
             "TextBlock.card-title" (page headers) and this file's ".family-primary
             TextBlock.card-title" were BOTH StyleTrigger tier (a class on each side), so the tie
             went to registration order — App.axaml's rule registered later and won, and every
             sensor title rendered as a page header. Renamed to sidestep the collision entirely
             rather than relying on include order to fix it.
           - The Home tile hover rules below (whole-branch review). App.axaml's
             "material|Card.interactive:pointerover" and this file's "material|Card.family-{F}"
             are again both StyleTrigger tier, so with this include registered BEFORE the hover
             block the hover rule won and repainted a themed tile with CardBackgroundHoverBrush.
             The StyleInclude now sits after App.axaml's hover blocks, and the explicit
             "family-{F}.interactive:pointerover" rules say what a themed tile does on hover
             (keeps its family body) instead of leaving it to whichever rule happens to be later.
         Never reuse a part class name here without checking
         `git grep -n "\.card-" remex.desktop/App.axaml remex.desktop/Styles remex.desktop/Themes`
         first — a collision is silent, not a compile error or a binding warning.

         "card-plate" (value plates) and "card-legend-plate" (the dual-metric legend plate) are
         split for the same reason .3.2's first pass got the family-custom alpha wrong: the two
         were never the same opacity. Family (non-custom) styles paint both from the identical
         CardPlate{F}Brush, but family-custom is still hand-authored hex, and the value plates were
         always 0.8 while the legend plate was always 0.78 — collapsing them to one class collapsed
         the alpha too and broke Acceptance 4 (an overridden card must be pixel-identical to today).

         ONE DICTIONARY SERVES THREE HOSTS. Selectors below are class-only ancestors
         (".family-primary TextBlock.sensor-title"), which match any host type per Avalonia's
         selector rules — so the same rule paints the canvas ctrl:DraggableCard, the Home
         material:Card tile and the tray strip's StackPanel alike. Every setter is a
         DynamicResource, so a palette or GlassOpacity change repaints every card with no
         per-card subscriptions (see ThemeService.ApplyCustomizationCore).

         WHY A VALUE SET DIRECTLY ON AN ELEMENT WOULD BREAK THIS. A local attribute
         (Foreground="{Binding …}") always beats a Style setter regardless of selector
         specificity, so every part that must repaint per family lost its inline colour
         attribute in CanvasView.axaml / HomeView.axaml / TrayFlyoutWindow.axaml and gained a
         part class instead — that move is the whole trick this file depends on.

         family-custom IS THE EXCEPTION, ON PURPOSE. An overridden card keeps today's hex
         bindings (Sensor.Theme.* / Theme.*) inside these Style setters — a Binding inside a
         Setter resolves against the TARGET element's DataContext, which is why the same part
         class needs two different binding paths across hosts: the canvas card's DataContext is
         CanvasCardViewModel (bindings go through ".Sensor"), while the Home tile and tray strip
         bind SensorViewModel directly (no prefix). family-custom sets no card Background —
         an overridden card keeps CardBackgroundBrush, exactly as before this spec. -->

    <!-- ─── Primary ─── -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-primary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-primary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Home tile hover (whole-branch review): StyleTrigger tier, to outrank App.axaml's
         "material|Card.interactive:pointerover" — see the header comment above. -->
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-primary.interactive:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary TextBlock.sensor-title">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary TextBlock.card-value">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary TextBlock.card-value-2">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary TextBlock.card-unit, .family-primary TextBlock.card-legend-name">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkDimPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary Border.card-pill, .family-primary Border.card-plate, .family-primary Border.card-legend-plate">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardPlatePrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="SecondaryAccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoPrimary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary Border.card-legend-1">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary Border.card-legend-2">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-primary mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesPrimaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ─── Secondary ─── -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-secondary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodySecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-secondary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodySecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-secondary.interactive:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodySecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary TextBlock.sensor-title">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary TextBlock.card-value">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary TextBlock.card-value-2">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary TextBlock.card-unit, .family-secondary TextBlock.card-legend-name">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkDimSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary Border.card-pill, .family-secondary Border.card-plate, .family-secondary Border.card-legend-plate">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardPlateSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesSecondary}"/>
        <Setter Property="SecondaryAccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoSecondary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary Border.card-legend-1">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary Border.card-legend-2">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-secondary mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ─── Tertiary ─── -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-tertiary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-tertiary">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-tertiary.interactive:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary TextBlock.sensor-title">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary TextBlock.card-value">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary TextBlock.card-value-2">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary TextBlock.card-unit, .family-tertiary TextBlock.card-legend-name">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkDimTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary Border.card-pill, .family-tertiary Border.card-plate, .family-tertiary Border.card-legend-plate">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardPlateTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTertiary}"/>
        <Setter Property="SecondaryAccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoTertiary}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary Border.card-legend-1">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary Border.card-legend-2">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-tertiary mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTertiaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ─── Neutral ─── -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-neutral">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-neutral">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-neutral.interactive:pointerover">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardBodyNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral TextBlock.sensor-title">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral TextBlock.card-value">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral TextBlock.card-value-2">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral TextBlock.card-unit, .family-neutral TextBlock.card-legend-name">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardInkDimNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral Border.card-pill, .family-neutral Border.card-plate, .family-neutral Border.card-legend-plate">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardPlateNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesNeutral}"/>
        <Setter Property="SecondaryAccentColor" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoNeutral}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral Border.card-legend-1">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral Border.card-legend-2">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesTwoNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector=".family-neutral mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource CardSeriesNeutralBrush}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ family-custom: canvas host (DataContext = CanvasCardViewModel, bindings go through
         ".Sensor") ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom TextBlock.sensor-title" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.LabelColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom TextBlock.card-value" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.ValueColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom TextBlock.card-value-2" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Sensor.SecondaryAccentHex, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom TextBlock.card-unit, ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom TextBlock.card-legend-name" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.UnitColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Border.card-pill" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.CardBackground, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToTranslucentBrushConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=0.8}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Value plates were always 0.8; the legend plate below was always 0.78 — restored as two
         classes after fix round 1 found the earlier single "card-plate" class had collapsed the
         two alphas into one and silently changed the value plate's look on an overridden card. -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Border.card-plate" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.CardBackground, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToTranslucentBrushConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=0.8}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Border.card-legend-plate" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.CardBackground, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToTranslucentBrushConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=0.78}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.AccentColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToColorConverter.Instance}}"/>
        <Setter Property="SecondaryAccentColor" Value="{Binding Sensor.SecondaryAccentHex, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToColorConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Border.card-legend-1" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.AccentColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Border.card-legend-2" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Sensor.SecondaryAccentHex, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- The alert bell's resting icon colour (CanvasView.axaml's Button.alert-bell mi|MaterialIcon)
         moved here rather than staying inline, so CanvasView.axaml carries no per-theme colour
         binding at all — the family case is covered by ".family-{F} mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon"
         above via the icon's own "card-icon" class. -->
    <Style Selector="ctrl|DraggableCard.family-custom Button.alert-bell mi|MaterialIcon" x:DataType="vm:CanvasCardViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Sensor.Theme.UnitColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ family-custom: Home pinned tile (DataContext = SensorViewModel directly, no prefix) ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom TextBlock.sensor-title" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </Style>
    <!-- Spec B §5 (RemEx-4kv0g.3.2 review): the tile's value/unit follow on<F>Container too — an
         overridden tile keeps its own hex, same as the canvas card's card-value/card-unit. -->
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom TextBlock.card-value" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Theme.ValueColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom TextBlock.card-unit" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Theme.UnitColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToBrushConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom Border.card-pill" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{Binding Theme.CardBackground, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToTranslucentBrushConverter.Instance}, ConverterParameter=0.8}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{Binding Theme.AccentColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToColorConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="material|Card.family-custom mi|MaterialIcon.card-icon" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{Binding Theme.AccentColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToColorConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>

    <!-- ═══ family-custom: tray flyout strip (DataContext = SensorViewModel directly) ═══ -->
    <Style Selector="StackPanel.tray-sensor.family-custom ctrl|SparklineControl.card-spark" x:DataType="vm:SensorViewModel">
        <Setter Property="AccentColor" Value="{Binding Theme.AccentColor, Converter={x:Static conv:HexToColorConverter.Instance}}"/>
    </Style>
</Styles>
